## Run order

P1 cases first, then P2, P3; out-of-scope guards and regression cases are part of the run.

## Per case

```
<CASE-ID>  @ <revision>  env <environment>  role <role>
Steps executed: <as written; note any deviation>
Observed:       <what the tool showed / returned>
Persistence:    <reload / read-back result>
Evidence:       <files under {{evidence_path}}>   stubbed: <provider | no>
Result:         PASS | FAIL | BLOCKED (<reason>) | NOT_RUN (<reason>)
```

## Evidence

- Saved under `{{evidence_path}}` with names `{{evidence_naming}}` <!-- GEN: e.g. <CASE-ID>-<state>.png; some tools only write inside the workspace -->
- Screenshots of each required state; response bodies (redacted) for API cases; console/network excerpts.

## Results

Only `PASS` is a pass. A missing state, target, account or service is `BLOCKED` / `NOT_RUN` with the reason — never `PASS`.

